=== Europe ===
[[File:Bermuda Kite 01.jpg|thumb|[[Bermuda kite]]]]
In [[Greece]] and [[Cyprus]], flying kites is a tradition for [[Clean Monday]], the first day of [[Lent]]. In the [[British Overseas Territory]] of [[Bermuda]], traditional [[Bermuda kite]]s are made and flown at [[Easter]], to symbolise Christ's ascent. In [[Fuerteventura]] a kite festival is usually held on the weekend nearest to 8 November lasting for 3 days.

=== Polynesia ===
Polynesian traditional kites are sometimes used at ceremonies and variants of traditional kites for amusement. Older pieces are kept in museums. These are treasured by the people of Polynesia.

